From 304101ee9e9f75551e920a3861b6348502c42cab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shahrokh <design@cariblanco.best>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 03:36:45 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 13/13] layer split: a batch window's grouped rows cross the
 stage hand-off

A --batch-mtp window proposes two rows per slot - the confirmed token and its draft - so several consecutive
rows name the SAME slot.  The verifier refused exactly that with a layer split ("grouped slot rows do not
support a layer split yet"), and the refusal was fatal: the error rose to generate.cpp, the engine printed ERR
and exited 1, and the serve launcher restarted the engine on every request that admitted a slot.

The refusal was over-broad.  A stage split hands a window's residual on per ROW: row t of the window uses
hand-off row hbase + t, indexed the same on every stage, so grouped rows cross it unchanged - and the per-slot
state (GDN recurrence and conv history, the QSA K/V and indexer tail, the PLE history) was already handled per
contiguous run of rows of one slot.  Two bounds had assumed one row per slot and are corrected here:
stage_batch's range check now measures the window against the hand-off's own capacity (kVerifyMaxT rows, through
the pure batch_rows_fit_handoff in core/stage_plan.hpp), and every stage of a split is sized for the --batch-mtp
window, not only the first one (generate.cpp).  A window that genuinely does not fit is refused before any graph
is captured, so an ineligible combination is a start-up concern and never ends the engine.

Host-only: tests/core/stage_plan_test.cpp exercises batch_rows_fit_handoff (2 rows per slot over 1..4 slots, the
exact-fit, the overrun, a group past the buffer, the empty window).  Inert by default: without --batch-mtp the
window is max(--spec, --batch) and nothing changes.
